## Objective
- Find and report valid, original vulnerabilities in the latest version of Naver Whale browser eligible under scope.yml rules
- Primary hypothesis: Whale's custom sync/epoch-key authentication flow has an asymmetric request-response design where the client signs requests but performs zero verification on epoch-key responses

## Important Details
- Eligible: latest Whale browser bugs (must reproduce on latest version), third-party libs used ONLY by Whale, sync bugs
- Excluded: *.naver.com, *.navercorp.com, built-in extension web servers, URL preview spoofing, XSS Auditor bypass, IETab, SafeBrowsing FP/FN
- Secrets in commits: sha256 only, never raw
- Binary acquisition channel: `repo.whale.naver.com` confirmed accessible HTTP 200, hash-pinned `.deb` (sha256=`6458a95a…`); bypasses all prior cloudfront/APKMirror/Uptodown blocks
- Current desktop version: **v4.39.410.14** (same-day double release Aug 18 with Chromium 137→138 + login-server-error hotfix)
- Binary extraction path: `/tmp/opencode/whale_binary/extracted/opt/naver/whale/whale` (sha256=`10de323e6f89a5195f7e558259e849be75792e021decc2be8e61848b6653ce19`) — ephemeral, must re-extract after sandbox wipe
- NVD gap: 0 Whale CVEs published in 2026 (28 total, latest CVE-2025-69235 @2025-12-30), 8+ month disclosure gap confirmed static
- GitHub repo `naver/whale-browser-developers` is documentation-only (pushed 2019-09-23); 0 sync/crypto source files in any public branch

